From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flax <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
Subject: [PATCH] allowlist: add the OpenBMC OEM fan control command

phosphor-pid-control registers NetFn 0x2E, OEM group IANA 49871 (OpenBMC),
command 0x04 for zone fan control -- manual mode get/set, failsafe get, and
(with our phosphor-pid-control patch 0001) set PWM duty.  It was never in
ipmi-allowlist.conf, so every one of those subcommands was rejected with
completion code 0xD4 on the LAN channel, which is presumably why none of
them had ever been used.  The system interface bypasses this filter
entirely, so only remote callers were affected.

The channel mask is 0x7f7f rather than 0xff7f because this command writes:
the file's convention leaves bit 15 clear for anything the host should not
be able to drive, and the host has no business setting the BMC's fan speed.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform-specific]

---
--- a/ipmi-allowlist.conf
+++ b/ipmi-allowlist.conf
@@ -175,6 +175,7 @@
 0x2c:0x10:0xff7f   //<Group Extension>:<DCMI Get Temperature Readings>
 0x2c:0x11:0xff7f   //<Group Extension>:<DCMI Get DCMI Config Params>
 0x2c:0x12:0x7f7f   //<Group Extension>:<DCMI Set DCMI Config Params>
+0x2e:0x04:0x7f7f   //<OpenBMC OEM>:<Fan Control - manual mode / set PWM duty>
 0x2e:0x80:0x8080   //<OpenBMC OEM>:<IPMI Blob Transfer - allow BIOS SMBIOS push via KCS/SMM>
 0x2e:0xC0:0x7f7f   //<Intel OEM>:<Enable/Disable Node Manager Policy Control>
 0x2e:0xC1:0x7f7f   //<Intel OEM>:<Set Node Manager Policy>
